==== s2 lexer (spec §1, §2): source code points → token buffer ⍝
⍝ The token buffer is one array of ℤ after a sentinel. Slots 0 … 5 are the
scanner's registers: token count (breaths included), carried marks lo and ⍝
⍝ hi, reading index k, chunk start k0 (−1: none), line done. Records follow:
kind line col marks idx v1 v2 n, then the n code points of the text. ⍝
⍝ After the text come rn and the token's raw text as written (marks included,
in physical order), which the check pass shows in its traces. ⍝
⍝ Kinds: 1 name 2 tname 3 anti 4 inverse 5 int 6 real 7 trit 8 glyph
9 type 10 tprefix 11 bracket 12 string, and the addenda's 13 curse ⸸…, 14 exorcism ⛨… ⍝
⍝ (or the rite prefix ⛨), 15 blessing ✧ ✧✧, 16 vow ⍤⥀ ⍤ᚠ, 17 forbidden binding ⎔⸸ᵘ (v1: the curse
mask, the blessing's level, or 0 for a loop vow and 1 for a function's). idx −9 is none, −1 is ⁻, −2 is ⁺. ⍝
⍝ int: v1 value; real: v1/v2; type and tprefix: v1 prefix length, v2 slot of ⁽ or −1.

⎔ »tixe« ⟨ ℤ ⊸ ⟩ ᚡᚢ ⸫

⍝ ᚡᚤ a: a, or the enclosing function fails
⸫ ᚡᚤ ⟨ ⟦ ℤ ⟧ ⊸ ⟦ ℤ ⟧ ⟩ ⦃ ⦄

ᚡᚠ t: yes ↔ no ⍝
⦃ ⋔ ⦃ ⊕ ⦄ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⁼ ⦄ ⟨ ŧ ⊸ ŧ ⟩ ᚡᚠ ⸫
⸫ ᚡᚥ ⟨ ℤ ⊸ ℤ ℤ ⟩ ⦃ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄ ⦃ ⧗⁰ ⌁ ⧖ ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄ ⋔ ≶ ⍿¹ ⍿¹ ⦄
⦃ ⍿¹ ⍿¹ ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄ ⦃ ⧖ ⌁ ⧗⁰ ⦄ ⦄ ⟨ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ℤ ⟩ ᚡᚦ ⸫

