⍝ ==== s2 compile-time evaluator (spec §13 "eval"), as s1's eval.uh
The only interpreter in the toolchain: it runs past-tense calls (§9.2) and ⍝
⍝ decides prayers (§12) at compile time, and never appears in the output. It
evaluates pure code over ℤ, ŧ and ◌ of those, keeping integers within 2⁵³ ⍝
⍝ as s1 does. A value is [ty n ok role hasn] (hasn 0: a failed ◌ or a bare ◌).
Registers: 49 the first error (a string, −1: none), 50 unwinding a ◌ ⍝
⍝ failure, 51 steps taken, 52 call depth.

